## 7. `test/candlestick-horizontal.html` (new manual/visual test)

Upstream adds this page (257 lines) driving `testHelper.create`. It is a browser visual test, not a jest spec — add it if you want parity. The 10 cases it exercises (helper `createChartOption(chartType, xAxisType, yAxisType, encode, data, layout)` building `{xAxis, yAxis, series:[{type, encode, data, layout, itemStyle}]}`):

- `main0` candlestick, `xAxis.type='time'`, `encode:{x:0, y:[1,3,2,4]}`
- `main1` candlestick, `xAxis.type='category'`, `encode:{x:0, y:[1,3,2,4]}`
- `main2` candlestick, `yAxis.type='time'`, `encode:{x:[1,3,2,4], y:0}`  ← the crashing/blank case before the fix
- `main3` candlestick, `yAxis.type='category'`, `encode:{x:[1,3,2,4], y:0}`
- `main4` candlestick, `yAxis.type='category'`, `encode:{y:0}` ("horizontal candlestick")
- `main5` candlestick, `xAxis.type='category'`, `encode:{x:0}` ("vertical candlestick")
- `main6` same as main0 but with raw-array data
- `main7`/`main8`/`main9` boxplot with time x / time y / dual-time, `encode` `{x:5, y:[0..4]}` etc.

Data used: `daval = [{value: ["2017-10-24", 20, 34, 10, 38, 25]}, {value: ["2017-10-25", 40, 35, 30, 50, 42]}, {value: ["2017-10-26", 31, 38, 33, 44, 35]}, {value: ["2017-10-27", 38, 15, 5, 42, 28]}]`, plus `daray` (same rows as plain arrays) and `reversedaray` (date moved to index 5).

You can pull the file verbatim with:
`curl -o test/candlestick-horizontal.html https://raw.githubusercontent.com/apache/echarts/38449543ef14/test/candlestick-horizontal.html`
